  "prompt": "A factory uses a machine that produces wire at a rate of $18$ meters per minute. The factory needs to produce $750$ spools of wire, where each spool contains $240$ feet of wire. How many hours will it take for the machine to produce all the spools? (Use $1$ meter $= 3.28$ feet)",
  "choices": {
    "A": "$6,250123$",
    "B": "$125,00041$",
    "C": "$2,250,00041$",
    "D": "$180,000$"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "A",
  "explanation": "Total feet needed: $750 \\times 240 = 180{,}000$ feet. Convert to meters: $\\frac{180{,}000}{3.28} = \\frac{180{,}000}{\\frac{328}{100}} = \\frac{18{,}000{,}000}{328} = \\frac{2{,}250{,}000}{41}$ meters. Time in minutes: $\\frac{2{,}250{,}000}{41} \\div 18 = \\frac{2{,}250{,}000}{41 \\times 18} = \\frac{2{,}250{,}000}{738} = \\frac{125{,}000}{41}$ minutes. Convert to hours: $\\frac{125{,}000}{41} \\div 60 = \\frac{125{,}000}{2{,}460} = \\frac{6{,}250}{123}$ hours.",
